{
  "matching_rule": "(uses only periods and epochs, never flags; a star-ID match alone is never enough)\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nWritten after a first look at the queried catalogue rows, so it is not a blind pre-registration; it is\ndeliberately conservative (anything ambiguous stays unresolved).\nFor a DR24 TCE with period P, epoch T0 and duration D, and each DR25 KOI (or TCE) on the same KIC star:\n\n1. Period: ``r = P_dr25 / P``. Same period if ``|r - 1| <= 1e-3``. If ``r`` or ``1/r`` is within 0.1% of an integer\n   2..5 the object is recorded as a *period alias*, which is never a match.\n2. Epoch: for same-period objects, every DR24-predicted transit in the Kepler baseline (BKJD 120-1600) is compared\n   with the nearest DR25-predicted transit. ``max_sep_h`` is the largest separation; ``phase_offset`` is the epoch\n   offset as a fraction of the period (0.5 = the other object sits at the opposite phase, e.g. a secondary eclipse).\n3. Compatible if ``max_sep_h <= 0.5 * D`` (transit centres stay within half a DR24 duration for the whole mission).\n4. Exactly one compatible KOI = **matched**. No compatible KOI = **unresolved (no matching KOI)**. Several =\n   **unresolved (ambiguous)**. A same-period KOI whose epoch is incompatible is reported as such; if it is within\n   3 combined (propagated) standard errors the case is **unresolved (low-precision ephemeris)**.",
  "flag_meanings": {
    "koi_fpflag_nt": "Not Transit-Like: light curve not consistent with a transiting planet",
    "koi_fpflag_ss": "Stellar Eclipse: significant secondary event, transit shape or out-of-eclipse variability",
    "koi_fpflag_co": "Centroid Offset: signal source is a nearby star, from the image centroid",
    "koi_fpflag_ec": "Ephemeris Match: same period and epoch as another object; flux contamination"
  },
  "minor_flag_meanings": {
    "SWEET_NTL": "sinusoidal signal at the TCE period larger than the transit depth (not transit-like)",
    "SWEET_EB": "significant sinusoidal out-of-eclipse variability smaller than the depth (stellar eclipse)",
    "DEEP_V_SHAPED": "too deep and too V-shaped for a planet (stellar eclipse)",
    "HAS_SEC_TCE": "a subsequent TCE on the same star at the same period was identified as this signal's secondary",
    "MOD_SEC_ALT": "significant secondary event in the model-shift test (alternate detrending)"
  },
